  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Additional rainfall expected today into the \nweekend, though amounts are still uncertain. The rainfall could \nhelp provide some drought relief.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA low pressure system from the Great Lakes region tracks E this\nevening and tonight. This system helps develop a coastal low \nsystem, that will move NE along the New England coast. As of \nthis update, models agree that a slow frontal system will move \nalong the Gulf of Maine and into Downeast region this evening \nand tonight. Then as the low merges and intensifies, rain \namounts increase across the south.\n\nBy Saturday, the low will track into the Gulf of Maine and\nprogress NE into the Bay of Fundy. Ensemble and deterministic\nmodels show a better agreement with the track and timing, thus\nmore confidence in rain amounts. Amounts are looking at a chance\nfor 2.0-3.0 inches along the immediate coast, 1.0-2.0 inches in\nthe interior Downeast, 0.5-1 inches in the Central Highlands and\nsouthern Aroostook, and 0.1-0.5 in northern Aroostook.",
